  "independent_full_solution": {
    "task": "Globally order all nine historical mass values and determine the exact dimensionless Jupiter/Earth mass ratio.",
    "ordering_reasoning": "All coefficients are in [1,10). Values with smaller exponents are therefore smaller regardless of their coefficients. Exponent 23: Mercury 3.17 precedes Mars 6.40. Exponent 24: Venus 4.87 precedes Pluto 5.40 precedes Earth 5.98. Exponent 25 contains Uranus 8.70. Exponent 26: Neptune 1.03 precedes Saturn 5.69. Exponent 27 contains Jupiter 1.90. Merge these groups globally across both printed blocks.",
    "complete_increasing_order": ["Mercury", "Mars", "Venus", "Pluto", "Earth", "Uranus", "Neptune", "Saturn", "Jupiter"],
    "ratio_reasoning": "Divide the actual Jupiter mass by the actual Earth mass: (1.90*10^27)/(5.98*10^24)=(1.90/5.98)*10^(27-24)=(190/598)*1000=(95/299)*1000=95000/299. The kg units cancel. Since 299=13*23 and neither factor divides 95000, the fraction is reduced. The ratio is strictly between 317 and 318 because 299*317=94783 and 299*318=95082.",
